From 87cf32dd85f7d3c2f8a937c8e720a0e271e43130 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 11:49:27 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(import): divide the boundary edges of faces curved two
 ways finer

#2731 made the STEP chord report true: the highest kept facet edge times
the face kind's inside bound. The fit never splits a boundary edge, and the
kernel held those edges only to the pass tolerance, so each model with a
cone, sphere or torus face read 1.5 x the tolerance and became reduced
fidelity (fig8: 0.00749 mm, three shoulder_adaptive tests red).

Each shell edge is now divided before the pass by the largest inside bound
of its faces (step_fit::edge_divisors, CurveGuard::finer), once in the
shell's own polyline, so the shell stays closed. A cylinder carries its
finest rim's divisor to all its edges, so its wall still meshes rim to rim.
fig8 now reads 0.005 mm (full fidelity), 7822 -> 7974 facets.

Fixes #2754

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
